This firmware is a port of Stadiacast (https://github.com/jkfran/stadiacast), the Python
receiver for the Stadia Controller's Wi-Fi mode, and is licensed under the same MIT License
(see LICENSE). It was developed in a fork of that repository (dinoyoshi/stadiacast) and moved
here with its history on 2026-11-16. The protocol work it relies on is Stadiacast's.

The firmware encodes and decodes messages whose field numbers come from protobuf schemas that
Stadiacast reproduces from the Stadia Controller firmware (ota.282115), notably
webrtc_sdp.proto and input.proto. Those schemas, including the names in them, are Google's
work. They are not covered by the MIT License and the authors claim no rights in them. They
are used solely so that an independently created program can interoperate with the
controller's stock firmware.

firmware/core/opus/libopus is the Xiph.Org Opus codec, a git submodule under its own BSD
license (see the files in that submodule).

tests/fake_controller.py is from Stadiacast, with additions for the dongle (the microphone
echo); it runs against Stadiacast's Python package, installed by pyproject.toml.

